String: 
A string is a sequence of charcter liks "hello", "123", "ruby on rails"
String is immutable in Ruby, meaning that once a string is created, it cannot be changed.
But using the operation we can change the string as a mutable.

name = "Alice"
puts name.length
puts name.upcase
puts name[0]
puts name[0,3]


Common String Method:
str = "Ruby"
str.reverse
str.include?("u")
str.gsub("u". "o")

Array:
an array is an ordered collection of elements.
Can contain different data types like string, integer etc.

Example:
fruits = ["apple", "banana", "cherry"]
puts fruits[0]
puts fruits[1]
puts fruits.length

Commor Array Methods:
